{
  "id": "bitwise-and-of-numbers-range",
  "questionId": "bitwise-and-of-numbers-range",
  "slug": "bitwise-and-of-numbers-range",
  "title": "Bitwise AND of Numbers Range",
  "difficulty": "Hard",
  "category": "Bit manipulation",
  "patterns": [
    "bit manipulation"
  ],
  "lists": [
    "interview-150"
  ],
  "hints": [
    "as soon as the range [left, right] spans more than one value with a differing bit at some position, that bit position gets AND-ed with both a 0 and a 1 somewhere in the range, so it becomes 0 in the final answer - what does that tell you about which bits can possibly survive?",
    "only the bit positions where left and right agree, all the way from the most significant bit down to where they first differ, can survive - everything from the first differing bit downward is guaranteed to be zeroed out",
    "so the answer is exactly the common binary prefix shared by left and right, with all lower bits set to 0",
    "find that common prefix by right-shifting both left and right together, one bit at a time, until they become equal - count how many shifts it took, then left-shift the now-equal value back by that same count"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "trying to iterate through the entire range and AND every value, which times out for large ranges like [1, 2^31 - 1]",
    "shifting only one of left or right instead of both together when hunting for the common prefix",
    "forgetting to shift the final common-prefix value back left by the number of shift steps taken, and returning the shifted-down value instead"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given two integers `left` and `right` representing an inclusive range `[left, right]`.\n\n**Return the bitwise AND of every integer in that range.**\n",
    "constraints": [
      "0 <= left <= right <= 2^31 - 1"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "left equals right (the answer is just that single number)",
      "the range spans a power of two, forcing many low bits to become 0",
      "left = 0 (the answer is always 0 whenever left = 0 and right > 0)"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "left = 5, right = 7",
        "output": "4",
        "expectedOutput": "4",
        "explanation": "5 & 6 & 7 = 101 & 110 & 111 = 100 = 4"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "left = 0, right = 0",
        "output": "0",
        "expectedOutput": "0",
        "explanation": ""
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "left = 12, right = 15",
        "output": "12",
        "expectedOutput": "12",
        "explanation": "12, 13, 14, 15 are 1100, 1101, 1110, 1111 - AND-ing them all leaves 1100 = 12"
      }
    ],
